# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

## Repository

Read `.master/project.json` for stable project facts. Read only relevant `.master/docs/*` files when durable detail is needed.

## Commands

Use the install, test, build, and runtime commands recorded in `.master/project.json`.

## Non-Obvious Constraints

Repository evidence overrides stale Agent Master state. Keep durable project facts in `.master/docs/`, not in this adapter.

## Agent Master

Before continuing existing work:

1. Run `agent-master status --format json`.
2. Verify the recorded branch, commit, changed files, and working tree against git.
3. Continue from `next_action`.
4. Record important decisions and completed work with `agent-master checkpoint`.
5. Run `agent-master validate` before completion.
6. Checkpoint or hand off before ending the session.

Personal agent memory is supplementary. `.master/` is the shared cross-agent task record.
